   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Guessing something in the future",
     "texto": [
      "To say «I think it's going to…» or «it seems it's going to…», use **-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요**: 오다 → **올 것 같아요** (I think it's going to rain), 먹다 → **먹을 것 같아요** (I think I'm going to eat it), 재미있다 → **재미있을 것 같아요** (I think it will be fun).",
      "비가 **올 것 같아요** = I think it's going to rain."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Compared with -(으)ㄹ 거예요",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요** marks a guess or an impression and usually sounds less direct: 내일 비가 올 것 같아요 = I think it will rain tomorrow. **-(으)ㄹ 거예요** can express a plan or intention, or a prediction; on its own it does not guarantee certainty: 내일 비가 올 거예요 = it will rain tomorrow / it will probably rain. Context and words such as 아마 («probably») make the meaning clear."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
